{"id":"51b50bd771bfe2796b825aa3186c3d8674302166","axis":"silent","repo":"astral-sh/ruff","sha":"51b50bd771bfe2796b825aa3186c3d8674302166","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"crates/ty_python_semantic/resources/mdtest/class/super.md","lines":["@@ -773,9 +773,9 @@ super(B, B())[0]"," "," ### Generic base initializer"," ","-A generic base initializer can inherit both its own class's generic context and the subclass's","-generic context. The merged context is not the same as the subclass's enclosing context and should","-not be freshened as a recursive reference.","+Inside `Child[S]`, the base initializer expects a callback that accepts `S`, even though `S`","+defaults to `BaseException`. For example, a `Child[ValueError]` could pass a `ValueError` to the","+callback, so a callback that only accepts `OSError` is too narrow."," "," ```py"," from collections.abc import Callable","@@ -789,11 +789,14 @@ class Base(Generic[T]):","     def __init__(self, check: Callable[[T], bool] | None) -> None:","         self.check = check"," ","+def has_filename(error: OSError) -> bool:","+    return error.filename is not None","+"," class Child(Base[S], Generic[S]):","     def __init__(self, check: Callable[[S], bool] | None) -> None:","-        # Regression test: Freshening the merged context made this expect","-        # `Callable[[BaseException], bool]` instead of `Callable[[S], bool]`.","-        super().__init__(check)","+        super().__init__(check)  # ok","+        # error: [invalid-argument-type] \"Expected `((S@Child, /) -> bool) | None`\"","+        super().__init__(has_filename)"," ```"," "," ## Inferring `Self` in `super()` calls"],"additions":9,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/ty_python_semantic/resources/mdtest/generics/legacy/classes.md","lines":["@@ -1781,6 +1781,12 @@ reveal_type(generic_context(into_regular_callable(D)))"," reveal_type(D(1))  # revealed: D[int]"," ```"," ","+Through `super(D, D)`, the inherited `__new__` infers the specialization from its `cls` argument.","+","+```py","+reveal_type(super(D, D).__new__(D[str]))  # revealed: D[str]","+```","+"," ### Generic class inherits `__init__` from generic base class"," "," ```py","@@ -1805,6 +1811,24 @@ reveal_type(C(1, \"str\"))  # revealed: C[int, str]"," reveal_type(D(1, \"str\"))  # revealed: D[int, str]"," ```"," ","+Passing the bare class to `super` leaves the initializer unbound, so each call can infer its type","+arguments.","+","+```py","+def initialize(child: D[int, str]) -> None:","+    super(D, D).__init__(child, 1, \"value\")  # ok","+```","+","+Inside a class method, `super()` uses the specialization of `cls`. The initializer's `t` parameter","+expects `T`, which could be a type other than `int`.","+","+```py","+class Child(D[T, str]):","+    @classmethod","+    def initialize(cls, child: \"Child[T]\") -> None:","+        super().__init__(child, 1, \"value\")  # error: [invalid-argument-type] \"Expected `T@Child`\"","+```","+"," ### Generic class inherits `__init__` from `dict`"," "," This is a specific example of the above, since it was reported specifically by a user.","@@ -1899,6 +1923,57 @@ reveal_type(C(1, True))  # revealed: C[int]"," wrong_innards: C[int] = C(\"five\", 1)"," ```"," ","+### Calling a generic initializer on an existing instance","+","+An inherited initializer can infer its own type parameters from the arguments. Its explicit `self`","+annotation must also match the specialization of the receiver.","+","+```py","+from collections.abc import Callable","+from typing import Generic, TypeVar","+","+E = TypeVar(\"E\")","+A = TypeVar(\"A\")","+B = TypeVar(\"B\")","+T = TypeVar(\"T\", bound=str | int)","+","+class Either(Generic[E]):","+    value: E","+","+    def __init__(","+        self: \"Either[A | B]\",","+        first: type[A],","+        second: type[B],","+        default: A | B | Callable[[], A | B],","+    ) -> None: ...","+","+class TextOrNumber(Either[str | int], Generic[T]):","+    def initialize(self, default: T | Callab